    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9754624b0674e6d8dcd436e8011db47",
      "statement": "Rotation under ADR-0001 is manual by design (edit the Komodo Variable and redeploy the affected stack); automated rotation, lease/TTL, and fine-grained secret-access audit are explicit non-goals until the ADR's §7 revisit trigger fires (dynamic short-lived DB credentials wanted, mandated rotation/audit becomes required, or the footprint grows to multiple hosts or operators).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/ADR-0001-prod-secrets-management.md#L64-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b356bb556765f8cb0ce7ea8f15e3348f00dee3bb8cf677bcbe6f1b665f51bcc8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84eb14e14fe9494d95f710e1ea845d11",
      "statement": "The seven core production stacks (prod-auth, prod-mc-service, prod-mcm-bff, prod-movie-assistant, prod-audit, prod-observability, prod-vault) are declared as [[stack]] blocks in infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml, each carrying env_file_path = \".env.prod\" plus an environment block whose values are masked [[Variable]] tokens, so the committed TOML carries only tokens and never a secret value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml#L26-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d959375a0c6bc5dab8caafb176b7a8b9cc6c9e7fd6e2ca4505dda90b3b069053:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e0164b04cf74da8b0986146079e53a3",
      "statement": "Because Komodo writes a stack's environment block into that stack's env_file_path, adding a required ${VAR:?} reference to a prod compose is a change to that stack's declared inputs in stacks.toml; the break is invisible in CI (the compose files are valid and the dev stack supplies the value from its own generated env file) and only surfaces on a real Komodo deploy, which is why scripts/__tests__/komodo-stack-env.guard.test.mjs asserts every required variable a prod compose declares is supplied by its Komodo stack.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml#L1-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b062bd22ea6fcd113b5247c363812c1cef3c61ef9d0213d345a0dac0e6c03e8:"
